 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 529089,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p><img src=\"exercises/media/c1026d43b7113daf.jpg\" alt=\"The photo shows a round, green cell with a smooth, shiny surface. The cell resembles a balloon.\"></p>\n\n<p>The cell of the unicellular algae <i>Ventricaria ventricosa</i> is one of the largest known, reaching one to five centimeters in diameter. Like all single-celled organisms, <i>V. ventricosa</i> exchanges gases across the cell membrane. What adaptations would <i>V. ventricosa</i> likely have evolved related to its large size and ability to exchange materials with the outside environment?</p>\n",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1035764,
     "content_html": "adaptations that would decrease cell metabolism to meet the needs of the large cell"
    },
    {
     "id": 1035765,
     "content_html": "adaptations that would make the cell thicker, to reduce the loss of nutrients"
    },
    {
     "id": 1035766,
     "content_html": "adaptations that make diffusion or nutrient passage across their cell membrane more efficient due to the large size of the cell"
    },
    {
     "id": 1035767,
     "content_html": "adaptations that allow the cell to take in larger food objects using the components of its cell membrane"
    }
   ],
